  "limitations": [
    "Marker truthfulness requires compliant producers. JSON decoding, all-path normalization, marker placement, path resolver and replay dispatch are not Verus-refined to the model.",
    "A lying marker containing aliases can split identities. Stable namespace bindings, truthful legacy resolution and the earlier alias-safe collector policy remain required.",
    "No old log migration, compaction or bounded history memory; legacy/mixed histories retain legacy resolution work.",
    "The work-count model does not establish a wall-clock bound, bandwidth SLA or universal performance gain. Warm tails vary in this uncontrolled deployment.",
    "Intercepted readlink/readlinkat API counts are neither all filesystem calls nor kernel lookups/metadata-service RPC counts; compiled shims are built from hashed source per host.",
    "n=20 timing groups, nearest-rank p99=max, no filesystem cache eviction or controlled background load. Instrumented timings are kept separate.",
    "Data samples use 2 KiB/8 MiB files; existing sparse offsets cover 2 GiB/4 GiB/2 TiB. No new physical 100 GB/TB bandwidth run in this cycle.",
    "An initial local probe loaded an existing global package; its native hash identified the mismatch. Excluded from evidence, reinstalled into the isolated venv and reran with exact preceding-binary hash.",
    "Finite checks and selected actual Rust proofs do not establish absence of all bugs."
  ],
